<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Les Trois-Îlets</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Trois-Îlets</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Les Trois-Îlets is a commune on the south-west coast of Martinique, across the bay from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-de-france">Fort-de-France</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josephine-de-beauharnais">Joséphine de Beauharnais</a>, the first wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> and Empress of the French, was born on her family's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> estate of La Pagerie there in 1763. The estate is now a museum, and the commune is known for its pottery and as a tourist centre.</p></div>
